  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CDC Investigations and Technical Assistance: Cooperative Agreement for the Strengthening an the Development of Applied Epidemiology and Sustainable Public Health Capacity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) Investigations and Technical Assistance assists national and local health authorities and other health related organizations in controlling communicable diseases, chronic diseases and disorders, and other preventable health conditions. Investigations and evaluation of all methods of controlling or preventing disease and disability are carried out by providing epidemic aid, surveillance, technical assistance, consultation, and program support; and by providing leadership and coordination of joint national, state, and local efforts.</narrative>
  </description>
